From d7fb062e427aa7631270a3746c9385d69acbfb0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:19:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): persist first-send envelopes across uncertain
 retries [daveey]

Problem: receipt expiry lets a fresh-HLC retransmission overwrite newer edits.
Why: the sender rebuilt hydrated payloads and clocks on every transmission;
only expiring server receipts tied those bytes to their mutation identity.
Root (happened): first-send ordering and payload were not durable. Root (not
caught): receipt-hit and cleanup tests missed lost-response plus restart and
competing-writer composition. Recurrence: known PR160 expiry-replay gap.

Persist outbox wire envelopes before network I/O and preserve synthetic parent
identity across uncertainty. Ack/prune cleans pending records. Definitively
rejected parents enter existing bounded retry/remap handling rather than
replaying cached refusal forever. Do not invent capture-time migration for
legacy attempted rows or silently rebuild corrupt/unknown envelopes.

Proof: original unchanged-base sender RED 2 failed/1 passed; fixed sender and
edge/compat controls GREEN; lease and neutral release selection 33 passed.
Synthetic-parent bounded rejection edge RED 1 failed/3 passed before repair.
Full scripts/check passed. Broader consumer selection and exact-head CI/review
remain required. This is sender-only: Worker child/delete/lifecycle replay
arbitration and supported deployment remain the service owner's open scope.
